{
  "note": "The ten monster types' vendor models and the hero's, as `champions monster bake` spawns them (MonsterModel.cs): the prefab and each clip by vendor GUID (rhythm_champions/manifest.json), the type's standing height in metres (the model is scaled to it), a flyer's hover over the ground, children to hide, the renderers it carries (weapons and shields skinned with the body, which its shatter flings like the struck part; a held weapon is carried anyway), weapons held in a humanoid fist (palm, pitch, yaw, roll: Fist's grip; onBone: on the hand bone as the prefab comes, as the trailer's knight held its shield), and each clip's role and annotations (loop; impact, end in seconds; strideM, the walk cycle's travel; liftM, a clip raised for flight). reviewPoses are the clips the review sheets show. A figure (the hero) is posed on the CPU from a rig its bake keeps and is drawn apart from the crowd (MonsterFigure); blade puts the trailer's crystal blade in its right fist (CrystalBlade.cs). Carried over from the deleted edge-cut recipes (git b243e08b^:rhythm_champions/tools/recipes/edgecut/), which took them from game/'s roster.",
